WEBVTT

01:45.688 --> 01:46.523
Ko Mun-yeong.

01:49.692 --> 01:50.527
Ko Mun-yeong.

01:57.242 --> 01:58.118
Run.

01:58.743 --> 01:59.661
Run.

02:00.245 --> 02:01.955
- It's okay, Ko Mun-yeong.
- Run...

02:02.122 --> 02:03.581
- Please run. Go!
- It was just a dream.

02:03.665 --> 02:05.083
Please run. Go!

02:05.542 --> 02:07.502
Get out at once!

02:10.755 --> 02:11.756
Get lost.

02:15.301 --> 02:16.511
Leave at once.

02:25.562 --> 02:27.939
Okay, I won't leave.

03:26.623 --> 03:27.498
Why are you here?

03:30.293 --> 03:32.378
- You were burning up all night.
- So?

03:32.462 --> 03:33.963
You laid me down and played doctor?

03:38.551 --> 03:39.636
Just stay in bed.

03:40.011 --> 03:42.222
I'll drop Sang-tae off at his work
and pick up medicine.

03:42.722 --> 03:43.806
I didn't do anything wrong.

03:46.059 --> 03:47.852
That woman kept acting
as if she were my mom,

03:48.478 --> 03:50.104
so I told her that my mom died.
That's all.

03:51.689 --> 03:53.942
Right, okay.

04:11.626 --> 04:15.380
CHAPTER 7
THE CHEERFUL DOG

04:15.964 --> 04:18.007
Seongjin, Seongjin... Seongjin Plaza.

04:18.091 --> 04:20.051
Michuri Public Health Center.

04:20.134 --> 04:21.594
Seongjin, Seongjin... Seongjin Plaza.

04:21.678 --> 04:23.137
Michuri Public Health Center.

04:24.055 --> 04:27.100
Hiking... Hiking Trail Entrance.
Oeryong Bridge.

04:27.183 --> 04:28.935
Stop memorizing that.
Go wash up, Sang-tae.

04:31.562 --> 04:35.066
I'll take you to Jae-su's restaurant.
Let's head out together.

04:35.149 --> 04:37.568
I can go on my own. On my own.

04:38.236 --> 04:39.237
I know.

04:39.320 --> 04:40.697
But I have to go downtown too.

04:42.782 --> 04:44.659
You don't have to go
to the hospital today?

04:47.245 --> 04:48.079
I'm going to

04:49.747 --> 04:50.790
skip work today.

04:54.377 --> 04:56.838
- You can't leave like this.
- Rewind a little.

04:57.338 --> 04:58.172
Okay.

05:21.487 --> 05:24.324
The patient may go through conversion
and stop deluding herself,

05:25.033 --> 05:28.661
so let's keep an eye on her
and see what happens.

05:28.745 --> 05:29.829
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

05:30.747 --> 05:31.664
Sir.

05:31.956 --> 05:35.251
I think you have to take this up
with Ms. Ko Mun-yeong as well.

05:35.335 --> 05:38.921
First, let's find out
what she said to the patient.

05:39.005 --> 05:42.258
I bet she said something like,
"Your daughter is dead."

05:42.341 --> 05:44.052
So she fainted from the emotional shock.

05:44.135 --> 05:45.553
How would Ms. Ko know about that?

05:45.636 --> 05:48.973
Maybe Mr. Moon told her.

05:50.099 --> 05:52.560
- They're close, you know.
- No, they're not.

05:56.814 --> 06:00.068
You all know that he'd never disclose
any patient information.

06:03.404 --> 06:07.116
Anyway, we've been having problems nonstop

06:07.241 --> 06:09.452
ever since Ms. Ko started coming
to our hospital.

06:09.535 --> 06:11.245
We need to do something about this.

06:11.329 --> 06:12.747
Yes.

06:13.331 --> 06:14.207
I agree.

06:14.290 --> 06:15.792
Me too.

06:21.631 --> 06:24.801
Could you please stop scraping off
your dandruff and make a decision?

06:25.968 --> 06:28.513
Let's put her fairy tale class on pause

06:28.971 --> 06:31.599
until we find out what really happened.

06:31.682 --> 06:33.351
- Okay.
- Okay.

06:33.434 --> 06:34.936
Would that be all?

06:35.853 --> 06:37.605
Tell Mr. Moon
that I'd like to speak with him.

06:37.688 --> 06:39.398
He didn't come in today.

06:39.649 --> 06:41.859
He called earlier and said
that something came up at home.

06:42.401 --> 06:43.653
Oh, really?

06:55.498 --> 06:57.875
Sang-tae, how do you feel
about quitting the job

06:59.127 --> 07:00.378
at Jae-su's restaurant?

07:01.754 --> 07:04.757
You've been doing so many things
ever since we moved here.

07:06.884 --> 07:08.511
Drawing the mural at the hospital

07:08.594 --> 07:10.179
and selling pizza at Jae-su's restaurant.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.056
When you start
working on the illustrations...

07:14.267 --> 07:15.435
You'll be too busy.

07:15.852 --> 07:17.562
Being busy isn't a bad thing.

07:19.480 --> 07:20.606
Right, it's not a bad thing.

07:21.190 --> 07:23.526
But if you're too busy,
you might fall ill.

07:24.068 --> 07:26.737
- You may ache all over--
- Like a dog.

07:27.822 --> 07:28.656
What?

07:28.739 --> 07:31.159
You whimper like a dog at night
when you're ill.

07:31.242 --> 07:35.037
I don't do that, but you always
whimper like a dog when you sleep.

07:38.749 --> 07:39.792
Hello.

07:43.004 --> 07:45.006
What? I do that?

07:46.716 --> 07:47.675
That's odd.

07:48.968 --> 07:50.344
I'm not ill.

07:50.928 --> 07:52.430
I no longer work multiple jobs,

07:53.181 --> 07:55.266
so I feel perfectly fine.

07:56.225 --> 07:57.727
It's because your heart is aching.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.105
"Your body is honest.

08:01.731 --> 08:03.816
When you're in physical pain, you cry.

08:05.401 --> 08:09.614
But the heart is a liar.
It stays quiet even when it's hurting.

08:10.531 --> 08:12.366
Then when you're asleep,

08:12.450 --> 08:16.162
you finally weep and whimper like a dog."

08:27.757 --> 08:29.133
You like this book that much?

08:29.217 --> 08:33.137
Yes, The Cheerful Dog by Ms. Ko Mun-yeong.

08:33.221 --> 08:34.639
"Written by Ko Mun-yeong.

08:35.556 --> 08:37.099
Once upon a time..."

08:42.271 --> 08:43.397
Oh, we're not open yet...

08:47.276 --> 08:49.820
You jerk! You moved in with her
without discussing it with me.

08:49.904 --> 08:51.280
Did you think I'd be happy to--

08:54.325 --> 08:55.243
Hello?

08:56.327 --> 08:57.370
Yes.

08:58.538 --> 08:59.455
Let's talk later.

09:00.164 --> 09:02.166
- Right.
- Later? When?

09:02.250 --> 09:04.669
Hey! I'll be waiting, okay? Hey!

09:05.586 --> 09:07.004
- Hi, Jae-su.
- Goodness!

09:08.130 --> 09:09.715
Jeez. Hi, Sang-tae.

09:10.841 --> 09:12.885
She's not feeling well.

09:12.969 --> 09:17.181
Come on. When did she start
feeling unwell? And what are the symptoms?

09:17.265 --> 09:20.142
I need details!

09:20.810 --> 09:23.271
She's not answering my calls.
I'm getting a bad feeling.

09:23.437 --> 09:25.773
- I was worried all night--
- I'll tell her to give you a call.

09:26.691 --> 09:27.650
I have to go.

09:27.733 --> 09:30.194
GEUKJIN PHARMACY

09:33.531 --> 09:36.367
I can't believe
he hung up on me like that.

09:37.868 --> 09:40.037
Gosh, that heartless prick.

09:40.663 --> 09:41.497
Right?

09:42.456 --> 09:45.960
He would be way more attractive
if he was more relaxed.

09:46.127 --> 09:48.004
He's too uptight. What a shame.

09:48.087 --> 09:50.172
But physically, he's totally my type.

09:52.717 --> 09:56.679
You have to tiptoe around me
every single day,

09:56.762 --> 09:58.931
yet you're still so dull-witted.
How's that possible?

10:01.684 --> 10:04.604
Right? Had I been quick-witted,

10:04.687 --> 10:07.398
I wouldn't have trusted you
and come all the way here.

10:08.065 --> 10:09.191
Sorry about that.

10:10.526 --> 10:11.485
It's all my fault.

10:14.655 --> 10:16.490
I have to go check in on Mun-yeong.

10:17.617 --> 10:19.577
Settle up with this

10:20.161 --> 10:24.081
and get a latte or something
at a cafe somewhere.

10:27.793 --> 10:29.253
See you later, sir!

10:37.470 --> 10:38.888
That son of a bitch.

10:42.016 --> 10:43.851
Maybe I should side with Ko Mun-young.

10:43.934 --> 10:46.354
He that would eat the fruit
must climb the tree.

10:56.238 --> 10:57.782
Mamma mia!

11:10.461 --> 11:12.922
MR. LEE

11:22.723 --> 11:25.393
Long hair suits you
because you take after me.

11:26.602 --> 11:28.270
Never cut your hair short.

11:29.063 --> 11:30.064
But I'm tired of it.

11:33.192 --> 11:34.735
You have to listen to Mom, right?

11:36.028 --> 11:37.071
Answer me.

11:41.951 --> 11:42.868
Answer me!

11:45.121 --> 11:45.996
Yes,

11:47.873 --> 11:48.958
Mom.

12:07.768 --> 12:08.686
Please...

12:10.521 --> 12:11.564
Save me!

12:34.003 --> 12:35.004
Mun-yeong.

12:36.464 --> 12:37.798
Are you okay?

12:38.507 --> 12:40.092
I want to cut it,

12:41.927 --> 12:43.554
but I just can't.

12:45.181 --> 12:46.015
Cut what?

12:47.600 --> 12:48.434
My mom.

12:54.398 --> 12:55.691
Did you get sleep paralysis again

12:56.859 --> 12:58.444
because of that hallucination?

13:00.571 --> 13:01.614
Since when?

13:02.823 --> 13:05.034
When did you start
experiencing them again?

13:10.247 --> 13:11.790
The first day back here.

13:16.795 --> 13:19.590
You can't stay here.
I'm taking you back to Seoul now.

13:19.673 --> 13:22.843
I'm warning you.
Do not touch any of my stuff.

13:23.469 --> 13:25.262
Then let me warn you as well!

13:25.638 --> 13:27.556
I'm going to knock you out if I must,

13:27.640 --> 13:29.099
so don't stop me.

13:29.225 --> 13:32.019
I know that you'll be destroyed

13:32.102 --> 13:34.188
if those hallucinations
start haunting you again.

13:34.271 --> 13:36.524
So I absolutely cannot let you stay here.

13:36.607 --> 13:38.067
I've had a bad feeling ever since

13:38.359 --> 13:41.695
you talked about those red shoes
and moved here with that caregiver guy.

13:41.820 --> 13:44.365
You two should've never gotten involved--

13:48.619 --> 13:50.120
I've known you for ten years.

13:51.705 --> 13:52.873
I at least know this much.

13:58.796 --> 14:00.214
- Follow me.
- Let go!

14:00.297 --> 14:01.549
Come with me!

14:01.632 --> 14:02.925
- Let go!
- Come on.

14:03.008 --> 14:05.219
Let go of my hand.
Do you have a death wish?

14:05.302 --> 14:07.304
Sure, I'll die so you can live.

14:07.388 --> 14:09.181
And you must leave this house to live.

14:10.516 --> 14:11.725
Come on. Let's go.

14:14.937 --> 14:16.438
- Jeez.
- I'm not leaving.

14:17.398 --> 14:18.774
- Let go.
- I'm not leaving.

14:18.857 --> 14:20.067
- Let go.
- I won't even budge.

14:20.150 --> 14:22.486
You have to leave. Let go already.

14:23.779 --> 14:25.614
What the hell are you doing?

14:29.159 --> 14:30.160
You stay out of this.

14:30.244 --> 14:31.912
Mun-yeong and I...

15:12.077 --> 15:13.037
Will you get off me?

15:16.332 --> 15:17.499
Well...

15:18.292 --> 15:19.668
I'm taking her.

15:20.252 --> 15:22.463
You should pack up
and get out of this place too. Hurry!

15:23.130 --> 15:24.006
Let's go, Mun-yeong.

15:25.549 --> 15:27.217
Did you just hit me?

15:27.301 --> 15:28.719
- Kick him out at once.
- Hey.

15:29.303 --> 15:31.013
Why are you acting all weak?

15:31.096 --> 15:33.140
Dragging her against her will
is considered violence.

15:33.223 --> 15:34.058
What?

15:34.141 --> 15:35.601
You used it first,
so I can use it too, right?

15:40.439 --> 15:41.440
Hey, that hurts!

15:47.488 --> 15:48.906
Hey, wait!

15:50.032 --> 15:50.866
Mun-yeong.

15:51.909 --> 15:54.370
Hey, that guy doesn't know much about you!

15:55.245 --> 15:57.915
I'm the only one who can
protect and look after you.

15:57.998 --> 15:58.832
Mun-yeong?

16:08.509 --> 16:09.593
Damn it!

16:17.601 --> 16:19.436
Keep the door locked
when you're here alone.

16:20.062 --> 16:22.064
- If anyone can--
- Do you think someone will harm me?

16:22.856 --> 16:25.567
Come on. Me?
It'll probably be the other way around.

16:32.992 --> 16:33.951
Still, keep it locked.

16:34.952 --> 16:36.578
You said scary things can happen

16:37.913 --> 16:39.123
when you let your guard down.

16:42.668 --> 16:43.627
Take this fever reducer.

16:44.253 --> 16:46.672
If I took crap like this
every single time I need to cool down,

16:47.006 --> 16:48.924
I'd already be a junkie.

16:49.758 --> 16:51.135
This won't cool me down.

16:53.846 --> 16:55.139
Then get some fresh air.

17:26.295 --> 17:28.255
I like what you prescribed me.

17:29.256 --> 17:30.674
- Where do you want to go?
- A motel.

17:34.678 --> 17:35.971
What do you want to eat?

17:36.055 --> 17:37.181
You.

17:44.229 --> 17:45.439
Are you going to keep this up?

17:46.315 --> 17:49.276
Okay, fine. I'll follow
my doctor's instructions today.

17:49.818 --> 17:51.111
What will you feed me?

17:51.195 --> 17:53.072
Thank you. Enjoy.

17:54.531 --> 17:55.616
This looks good.

17:56.784 --> 17:57.659
Sang-tae.

18:04.917 --> 18:07.961
No, don't say that. You have to say
"come on" to call me over.

18:10.756 --> 18:13.425
When someone says "later,"
what does it actually mean?

18:13.509 --> 18:14.760
Sometime before you die.

18:16.011 --> 18:17.513
What? Before you die?

18:17.596 --> 18:18.639
Yes.

18:19.723 --> 18:20.808
No way.

18:21.183 --> 18:24.686
We've known each other for so long.
He'd never do that to me.

18:24.770 --> 18:27.022
For how long? How much?
1,000 won? 2,000 won?

18:27.106 --> 18:28.982
I met you and Gang-tae

18:29.358 --> 18:30.984
when I was only 16.

18:31.068 --> 18:32.111
At Jae-su's Fried Chicken.

18:32.194 --> 18:34.488
That's right.
My parents had a fried chicken place,

18:34.571 --> 18:36.615
and Gang-tae worked there part-time
and lived with us.

18:36.824 --> 18:40.077
I'm a year older than him,
but he never treated me as such.

18:40.160 --> 18:42.913
And he always gave you all the drumsticks.

18:42.996 --> 18:45.207
I only eat drumsticks.

18:45.290 --> 18:46.458
I envied you.

18:47.251 --> 18:49.378
I wished I'd also had
a little brother like Gang-tae.

18:50.254 --> 18:53.132
So one day, I said to him, "Think of me
as your brother, you little prick."

18:54.091 --> 18:56.760
Then he said,
"I don't need another brother."

18:56.844 --> 18:59.763
- I'm his real brother.
- That was when I realized this.

19:02.266 --> 19:05.185
"He needs a friend, not another brother."

19:05.769 --> 19:07.688
I need a friend too.

19:18.407 --> 19:19.449
It's good.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.660
I guess what I needed was food,
not medicine.

19:22.369 --> 19:25.747
This is awakening my ferociousness.
I feel much better now.

19:28.125 --> 19:29.585
- It's not cooked yet.
- It's okay.

19:29.668 --> 19:31.044
I have a lot of internal heat.

19:34.506 --> 19:36.216
I can't control myself around food.

19:36.800 --> 19:38.343
I'm hungry no matter how much I eat.

19:39.386 --> 19:41.013
Is it because I'm an empty can?

19:49.062 --> 19:50.147
I'm sorry.

19:52.482 --> 19:53.317
I was just

19:54.735 --> 19:55.611
talking nonsense then.

19:56.737 --> 19:58.197
- It's true though.
- No.

20:01.408 --> 20:02.367
You're not an empty can.

20:04.870 --> 20:05.704
Then what am I?

20:07.706 --> 20:08.540
Well...

20:10.876 --> 20:11.710
A thug?

20:14.296 --> 20:15.547
Eat up. It'll burn.

20:19.384 --> 20:20.677
As you may already know,

20:20.761 --> 20:23.055
I only sold chicken after that.

20:23.138 --> 20:25.724
Fried, steamed, sweet and sour,
drumsticks, and even chicken feet.

20:25.807 --> 20:27.476
- Why do you think I did that?
- Chicken head.

20:28.936 --> 20:31.605
That's the only part you didn't sell.
The chicken head.

20:32.356 --> 20:33.190
That's right.

20:34.149 --> 20:36.360
- The chicken head isn't sellable.
- That's right.

20:38.195 --> 20:41.281
You know, I didn't want to sell chicken.
I was even sick of the smell.

20:41.365 --> 20:44.159
But it was the only kind of business
I could open and close quickly.

20:44.243 --> 20:46.495
Because I didn't know
when my friend had to move again,

20:46.578 --> 20:48.205
I kept selling chicken.

20:48.664 --> 20:50.332
But this time, it felt different.

20:50.832 --> 20:53.293
I felt that he might settle down
in Seongjin City.

20:53.627 --> 20:56.755
So I put together all the money I had
and even took out a loan

20:56.838 --> 21:00.092
to finally open a different kind
of business. No more chicken.

21:00.175 --> 21:01.260
But he...

21:02.469 --> 21:04.513
He left me.

21:04.972 --> 21:05.973
Why?

21:07.140 --> 21:08.976
Because he likes

21:09.434 --> 21:12.479
that lunatic Ko Mun-yeong
more than me, his friend of 15 years.

21:13.230 --> 21:15.148
- No, that's not why.
- That is why!

21:15.232 --> 21:16.066
It was because of me.

21:16.650 --> 21:19.236
Gang-tae followed me
because of my contract with her.

21:19.319 --> 21:21.321
It's like a BOGO deal.

21:23.657 --> 21:26.785
Don't trust Gang-tae too much.

21:27.077 --> 21:28.412
You might end up like me.

21:28.495 --> 21:29.871
Like you?

21:31.290 --> 21:33.250
Like the dog that chased the chicken.

21:33.834 --> 21:34.668
A dog?

21:41.383 --> 21:42.426
A dog!

21:50.058 --> 21:52.978
That was loud. I'm sorry. That was loud.

21:55.272 --> 21:57.691
- Hello, Mr. Moon.
- Hello!

22:07.659 --> 22:10.287
By the way, why aren't you eating?
You're just feeding me.

22:11.413 --> 22:12.873
I'm not really hungry.

22:12.956 --> 22:14.291
Have you ever slept with a woman?

22:17.753 --> 22:20.005
- Never?
- Why are you suddenly talking nonsense?

22:20.088 --> 22:21.923
You seem to have no desires whatsoever.

22:22.049 --> 22:25.469
You don't want to eat, have,
or do anything.

22:25.552 --> 22:26.428
You always look apathetic.

22:26.511 --> 22:28.263
- I'm not apathetic.
- Then what?

22:33.060 --> 22:34.478
I'm just suppressing myself.

22:35.103 --> 22:35.937
Why?

22:37.773 --> 22:40.859
You do everything you want to do,
but that's not the case for most people.

22:41.860 --> 22:44.029
Don't suppress yourself.
It shouldn't be that hard.

22:52.871 --> 22:54.247
Your safety pin...

22:55.415 --> 22:56.416
Shall I pull it for you?

22:59.336 --> 23:00.545
I'm curious

23:01.129 --> 23:03.548
to see what will happen
if you don't suppress yourself.

23:09.221 --> 23:10.263
Hey, Byeol.

23:10.806 --> 23:13.725
Patient Park Ji-hwan
falls from his bed easily,

23:13.809 --> 23:16.645
so make sure you help him if he needs
to go to the bathroom at night.

23:17.145 --> 23:19.731
I've already told Mr. O Cha-yong
everything he needs to know.

23:19.815 --> 23:21.900
Both of you should check on him
when doing your rounds.

23:21.983 --> 23:23.235
Okay, got it.

23:23.318 --> 23:26.113
And as for patient Kim Jeong-mi's
depression...

23:26.780 --> 23:27.739
Just a second.

23:30.617 --> 23:32.744
What's up? Sang-tae is here.

23:34.412 --> 23:36.623
He's chatting with the employee
from Ko Mun-yeong's publishing company.

23:36.706 --> 23:37.624
It's pissing me off.

23:42.879 --> 23:43.880
Who is it?

23:44.589 --> 23:45.715
It's nothing.

23:47.008 --> 23:49.719
- Where were we?
- Patient Kim Jeong-mi.

23:51.471 --> 23:53.640
That was a lengthy explanation.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.851
Let me sum it up for you.

23:55.934 --> 23:59.521
If Mr. Lee Sang-in's muse is
Ms. Ko Mun-yeong,

24:00.522 --> 24:02.691
then as the art director,
I get inspiration from you.

24:03.441 --> 24:05.735
You're my muse.
That was what I was trying to say.

24:07.445 --> 24:08.488
I see.

24:12.159 --> 24:13.368
That's why

24:14.619 --> 24:17.247
I brought some illustrations
you can refer to

24:17.330 --> 24:19.791
while working on Ms. Ko's next book--

24:23.253 --> 24:25.422
- Where are you going?
- I'm leaving for the day.

24:26.840 --> 24:28.633
It's rude to talk about irrelevant work

24:28.717 --> 24:30.594
at someone else's workplace.
Complete nonsense.

24:30.719 --> 24:35.265
Let's... Let's talk about it later.

24:35.348 --> 24:37.142
"Later" means sometime before you die.

24:37.225 --> 24:39.811
Jae-su, this is for you.

24:41.354 --> 24:43.607
- Bye, Sang-tae.
- Bye!

24:49.279 --> 24:50.572
What did he draw?

24:54.993 --> 24:57.579
The dog that chased the chicken.

25:01.833 --> 25:02.959
Why are we walking?

25:03.460 --> 25:04.294
What?

25:05.503 --> 25:07.464
It's nice to walk and enjoy the scenery.

25:08.465 --> 25:11.009
It helps you clear your mind
and lifts your spirits.

25:11.927 --> 25:14.763
Really? All I can think is that
my legs hurt and it's a waste of time.

25:15.722 --> 25:17.098
- Then shall we--
- Will you carry me?

25:17.766 --> 25:18.767
What?

25:20.602 --> 25:23.271
I wonder if Sang-tae is on his way home.

25:25.106 --> 25:26.233
I guess he's fine on his own.

25:27.859 --> 25:29.277
No! Jeez.

25:33.114 --> 25:35.700
So you should just focus on me.

25:36.993 --> 25:38.703
Okay, give it back.

25:41.373 --> 25:42.582
Come on. Give it back.

25:44.125 --> 25:45.335
Stop it.

25:56.096 --> 25:56.972
Are you

25:57.847 --> 25:59.266
holding me in your arms now?

26:07.148 --> 26:08.108
- Hey, Ju-ri.
- Hey.

26:11.194 --> 26:12.195
Ko Mun-yeong?

26:12.779 --> 26:14.864
My daring roommate
is in an awkward situation now,

26:15.448 --> 26:16.992
so I'm answering his phone. What's up?

26:19.869 --> 26:22.789
Well, he didn't come into work today.

26:27.544 --> 26:29.421
He took the day off to hang out with me.

26:29.754 --> 26:30.755
Bye.

26:48.982 --> 26:51.318
You didn't go to work
because you were worried about me?

26:52.819 --> 26:55.572
And you took me out on a date
to help me cool off?

26:57.365 --> 26:58.533
Who said this was a date?

26:59.617 --> 27:00.702
What was this, then?

27:00.785 --> 27:03.705
Are you flirting with me?
Or are you feeling it out?

27:03.788 --> 27:06.583
Are you just testing the waters?
Or are you playing me?

27:10.712 --> 27:11.588
Fine.

27:12.881 --> 27:13.882
Let's date.

27:18.595 --> 27:19.763
"Get lost."

27:21.890 --> 27:23.391
- What?
- "Get lost."

27:24.517 --> 27:26.811
Do you know how many times
you've said that to me?

27:27.604 --> 27:30.106
Even last night. And that day too.

27:31.691 --> 27:32.525
So what?

27:33.318 --> 27:34.778
But last night, it sounded like

27:36.446 --> 27:37.739
you were begging me not to leave.

27:39.783 --> 27:41.117
Last time, I ran away.

27:43.453 --> 27:44.371
But today,

27:46.790 --> 27:48.249
I thought I should stay with you.

27:53.755 --> 27:54.672
That's all it meant.

28:07.227 --> 28:08.978
Ko Mun-yeong, you heartless woman.

28:09.562 --> 28:11.398
All my organs are rotting

28:11.481 --> 28:14.442
because of the stress from
looking after you for the past ten years.

28:14.526 --> 28:17.404
How could you gang up on me
with that caregiver you just met

28:17.487 --> 28:19.697
and kick me out? Just how?

28:20.281 --> 28:24.077
Fine, you two heartless jerks
can live happily ever after.

28:25.620 --> 28:30.125
I'm going to find the kindest

28:30.500 --> 28:32.252
and sweetest woman on earth and--

28:32.335 --> 28:33.837
Shit!

28:34.587 --> 28:37.340
You're so loud. Damn it!

28:46.725 --> 28:50.019
Unrequited love is so hard. I give up!

29:01.281 --> 29:02.657
I guess you've never seen a woman

29:03.533 --> 29:05.368
who's heartbroken by unrequited love.

29:08.037 --> 29:08.872
Hey, Jae-su.

29:17.338 --> 29:18.298
Why

29:19.340 --> 29:21.009
can't it be me?

29:22.761 --> 29:24.387
Why that bitch?

29:27.223 --> 29:28.349
I can

29:30.226 --> 29:31.895
swear too.

29:33.396 --> 29:34.397
And I can also

29:36.274 --> 29:40.945
throw temper tantrums and smash things.

29:42.238 --> 29:43.072
I can

29:44.908 --> 29:47.410
stop acting nice all the time.

29:48.161 --> 29:49.370
And I can

29:51.456 --> 29:53.541
be a bitch too.

29:54.125 --> 29:58.379
Gosh, no. Not everyone can be a bitch.

30:08.681 --> 30:10.850
Who are you?

30:12.101 --> 30:13.645
Why cut me off?

30:14.395 --> 30:16.773
I'm not a weirdo.

30:18.191 --> 30:19.275
I'm...

30:20.735 --> 30:23.822
the CEO of SangSangESang Publishers.

30:24.489 --> 30:25.740
My name is Lee Sang-in.

30:26.366 --> 30:27.700
CEO LEE SANG-IN

30:47.637 --> 30:49.472
So it's all your fault.

30:49.556 --> 30:50.682
Don't cry.

30:50.890 --> 30:53.309
Do you know me?

30:53.393 --> 30:58.857
You should've talked Ko Mun-yeong
out of it.

30:59.566 --> 31:01.860
Then she wouldn't have moved here,

31:02.527 --> 31:05.071
and those two would've never met.

31:05.238 --> 31:07.866
Then I wouldn't have ended up like this.

31:09.742 --> 31:10.910
This is all on you.

31:11.995 --> 31:14.747
CEO Lee Sang-in.

31:15.456 --> 31:16.749
It's all your fault.

31:24.674 --> 31:26.718
Hold on, this voice...

31:27.677 --> 31:28.761
Are you...

31:29.721 --> 31:30.555
Hello?

31:30.638 --> 31:31.639
My tears.

31:31.723 --> 31:35.435
Mr. Lee. I'm Nam Ju-ri,
a nurse at OK Psychiatric Hospital.

31:37.020 --> 31:38.021
Nurse Nam Ju-ri?

31:49.991 --> 31:51.451
Last time, I ran away.

31:51.993 --> 31:54.954
But today,
I thought I should stay with you.

31:59.167 --> 32:00.126
What is it?

32:00.793 --> 32:01.753
Nothing.

32:10.219 --> 32:13.431
I had a nightmare last night.

32:16.142 --> 32:18.937
My nightmares are always about my mom.

32:20.939 --> 32:22.815
And when I wake up from the dream,

32:23.608 --> 32:26.653
I always feel like shit.

32:29.197 --> 32:30.323
But today,

32:32.742 --> 32:33.826
I don't feel so shitty.

32:48.007 --> 32:49.050
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

32:49.133 --> 32:50.969
But why? Just why?

32:51.052 --> 32:52.553
Why are they getting rid of the class?

32:52.637 --> 32:55.348
I liked her class because it was always
like a big smack in the head.

32:55.640 --> 32:57.517
I knew they'd get rid of it.

32:57.725 --> 32:59.435
I always questioned her state of mind,

32:59.519 --> 33:00.895
and she had a bad attitude.

33:00.979 --> 33:03.648
- Are you a school superintendent?
- I'm just a super old man, you punk!

33:03.731 --> 33:05.316
Stop hitting me in the head, will you?

33:05.566 --> 33:07.193
You said you like a big smack in the head.

33:07.902 --> 33:11.698
I did all the homework.
They can't get rid of this class.

33:12.031 --> 33:15.201
I was confident
that she'd compliment me this time.

33:15.660 --> 33:18.454
Are you possessed by a spirit
who wants to brag about doing homework?

33:18.538 --> 33:21.499
Why cry so early in the morning?
You're ruining my day.

33:21.582 --> 33:24.293
Why must you say such mean things
to A-reum so early in the morning?

33:24.877 --> 33:25.712
You two...

33:26.254 --> 33:27.755
Are you seeing each other or something?

33:27.839 --> 33:30.216
Let's go, A-reum. Just ignore her.

33:33.636 --> 33:36.389
I think they'll cause trouble
sooner or later.

33:46.482 --> 33:47.358
Did you eat?

33:47.650 --> 33:50.737
I had a fried egg, cubed radish kimchi,
three sausages, and soybean paste stew.

33:52.071 --> 33:53.364
What are you doing right now?

33:53.823 --> 33:55.283
I'm just sitting down.

33:56.451 --> 33:57.660
What about Ms. Ko?

33:58.036 --> 33:59.162
She's just sitting down.

33:59.454 --> 34:00.288
What?

34:17.638 --> 34:19.265
- Sang-tae.
- Yes?

34:20.433 --> 34:22.226
- Let's just have fun today.
- Okay.

34:33.821 --> 34:34.739
Come in.

34:38.451 --> 34:40.078
I heard you asked for me yesterday.

34:40.161 --> 34:42.955
Yes, there's something I want to ask you.

34:46.959 --> 34:48.795
Does Ms. Ko have a boyfriend?

34:52.298 --> 34:55.009
Well, I'm not sure.

34:55.551 --> 34:57.887
I have a son. I had him pretty late.

34:58.221 --> 35:00.807
Anyway, I'd like to introduce him to her.

35:01.933 --> 35:04.727
Don't worry. He takes after his mom,
so he looks nothing like me.

35:06.395 --> 35:08.981
What do you say? Should I do it or not?

35:12.110 --> 35:13.444
Why are you asking me?

35:13.528 --> 35:14.779
Because you live with her.

35:28.668 --> 35:31.921
Let's come separately next time.
People will get the wrong idea.

35:32.004 --> 35:34.006
When are you done?
Let's go home together. I'll wait.

35:34.090 --> 35:36.008
Does your car run on gasoline or diesel?

35:38.594 --> 35:41.430
I've been psychoanalyzing people
for so long

35:42.056 --> 35:46.018
that I can tell what their stories are
just by looking in their eyes.

35:46.602 --> 35:47.603
Why didn't you come in yesterday?

35:48.563 --> 35:50.690
I wasn't feeling well.

35:50.815 --> 35:52.275
You mean, Ms. Ko wasn't feeling well?

35:54.610 --> 35:55.444
Yes.

35:56.028 --> 35:57.905
Ms. Sun Byeol said

35:58.531 --> 36:01.951
Ms. Kang Eun-ja acted like she was her mom
and bugged her. Is that why?

36:05.413 --> 36:06.747
It seemed like Ms. Ko

36:08.291 --> 36:11.752
thought she was actually her mother
for a moment.

36:14.005 --> 36:17.425
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST
WRITTEN BY DO HUI-JAE

36:18.718 --> 36:20.970
Ms. Ko's mother 

36:21.804 --> 36:23.181
is the writer, Do Hui-jae.

36:25.850 --> 36:28.853
The day she finished the last book
of her fiction series,

36:29.979 --> 36:31.480
she vanished without a trace.

36:32.982 --> 36:36.569
Then she was registered as deceased
five years after she disappeared.

36:38.863 --> 36:40.698
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST

36:43.492 --> 36:45.328
You're always one step late.

36:50.291 --> 36:51.876
Some believed that she was still alive.

36:53.127 --> 36:54.670
There were a lot of rumors back then.

36:57.840 --> 36:59.508
Could she be alive?

36:59.592 --> 37:03.512
Then she wouldn't have kept
her readers waiting for almost 20 years,

37:03.596 --> 37:05.097
knowing how much they want

37:05.181 --> 37:08.434
to find out what ends up happening
to the Witch of the West.

37:12.396 --> 37:15.233
My nightmares are always about my mom.

37:17.318 --> 37:20.321
It must've been a big shock to Ms. Ko.
And I'm sure she misses her a lot.

37:21.822 --> 37:25.618
Maybe that's why she mistook
someone else for her mother.

37:25.701 --> 37:28.537
But what if she doesn't miss her?

37:29.997 --> 37:31.123
What if she fears her?

37:36.587 --> 37:39.131
COUNSELLING NOTE
PATIENT NAME KO DAE-HWAN

37:39.423 --> 37:41.676
HE GAVE SHORT, SIMPLE ANSWERS BUT DIDN'T
TRY TO AVOID ANSWERING THE QUESTIONS

37:55.106 --> 37:56.190
My wife?

37:57.775 --> 38:01.237
She was incredibly intelligent
and elegant.

38:02.655 --> 38:05.574
She loved our daughter very much.

38:07.076 --> 38:08.369
Maybe too much.

38:10.705 --> 38:12.290
Every night, she sang

38:13.332 --> 38:15.334
Oh My Darling, Clementine as a lullaby.

38:18.462 --> 38:19.380
I wonder

38:20.798 --> 38:25.344
if she knew
the true meaning behind the song.

38:39.358 --> 38:41.736
KO MUN-YEONG'S FAIRY TALE CLASS
PUT ON PAUSE TEMPORARILY

38:52.580 --> 38:54.040
- Ms. Park.
- What's the matter?

38:54.123 --> 38:56.167
Are you sad
that her class is put on pause?

38:58.377 --> 38:59.211
No.

39:02.381 --> 39:04.842
I think the patients are sad about it.

39:05.134 --> 39:06.927
They found the class
different and interesting.

39:08.554 --> 39:09.388
It is interesting.

39:11.766 --> 39:14.393
You should check out her books
when you have some time.

39:14.477 --> 39:16.896
No, I wouldn't be able
to relate to those stories.

39:18.439 --> 39:20.524
I like cruel and foolish love stories
or horror novels.

39:22.526 --> 39:24.111
I'll take some water to the padded room.

39:24.487 --> 39:26.614
All right. Thanks.
Take good care of the patient.

39:43.005 --> 39:44.131
Would you like some water?

39:51.514 --> 39:52.348
Well...

39:53.349 --> 39:54.266
About your daughter.

39:55.851 --> 39:57.937
You said you'd like me to meet her.

39:59.271 --> 40:00.898
Next time she visits you, I will--

40:00.981 --> 40:02.024
My daughter...

40:06.070 --> 40:07.154
is dead.

40:10.199 --> 40:11.242
Mom.

40:13.494 --> 40:16.205
How are you going to meet a dead girl?

40:22.837 --> 40:24.422
Even I can't meet her.

40:29.885 --> 40:30.886
Dr. Kwon!

40:32.012 --> 40:33.139
Darn it.

40:34.557 --> 40:37.184
Dr. Kwon, Ms. Kang Eun-ja is showing
conversion symptoms.

40:37.268 --> 40:39.145
What? Is she in the padded room?

40:39.228 --> 40:40.438
- Yes.
- Let's go.

40:44.191 --> 40:45.234
This shawl...

40:48.154 --> 40:49.780
It's very expensive.

40:53.284 --> 40:55.161
It's worth more than
hundreds of millions of won.

41:00.166 --> 41:01.208
I had never received

41:03.127 --> 41:05.546
something so expensive in my entire life.

41:07.798 --> 41:09.800
We barely managed to afford a living.

41:11.760 --> 41:13.721
But she spent her entire paycheck

41:14.722 --> 41:16.557
to buy me

41:18.851 --> 41:20.060
this shawl

41:21.020 --> 41:22.146
for my birthday.

41:23.939 --> 41:25.232
How much is this?

41:26.275 --> 41:27.526
How many zeros are there?

41:29.361 --> 41:31.655
Goodness! Go and get a refund right now!

41:32.323 --> 41:35.367
I got so furious and angry.

41:37.953 --> 41:40.831
So I slapped her really hard on her back.

41:42.958 --> 41:46.086
Do you think somebody like me
deserves something this expensive?

41:46.170 --> 41:47.922
I'm so sick

41:49.131 --> 41:51.967
and tired of you being like this.

41:57.473 --> 41:59.808
I don't remember much.

42:02.853 --> 42:03.979
But I remember saying this.

42:04.063 --> 42:07.608
I don't need
an immature daughter like you!

42:08.067 --> 42:10.903
I ended up telling her that I don't need

42:14.657 --> 42:15.908
a daughter like her.

42:35.219 --> 42:37.388
If I had known
she was going to die like that,

42:38.681 --> 42:39.557
I never would've

42:42.518 --> 42:44.603
said something so harsh.

42:48.274 --> 42:49.149
Never.

42:54.530 --> 42:56.156
- Gang-tae.
- Yes?

42:57.283 --> 42:59.660
You need to stay by your brother's side
until the day you die.

43:00.494 --> 43:01.745
That's why

43:03.455 --> 43:05.416
I gave birth to you.

43:16.552 --> 43:18.804
Why in the world did I say that to her?

43:24.226 --> 43:25.394
I'm such an idiot.

44:08.687 --> 44:09.688
Why do you look so sad?

44:10.439 --> 44:13.025
You're making it hard for me to get angry.

44:14.443 --> 44:15.527
You should also lie down.

44:28.374 --> 44:29.333
Jae-su.

44:30.084 --> 44:30.918
Yes?

44:32.711 --> 44:34.088
Do you think

44:36.840 --> 44:38.050
my mom also feels sorry

44:40.344 --> 44:41.845
for how she treated me?

44:45.683 --> 44:46.934
Do you think

44:50.312 --> 44:51.689
she regrets it?

44:54.733 --> 44:55.984
Is that what you want?

45:00.572 --> 45:01.407
Yes.

45:06.787 --> 45:07.621
No.

45:18.006 --> 45:21.427
Ma'am, why were you so mean to Gang-tae?

45:22.386 --> 45:24.430
Sang-tae wasn't your only son!

45:24.513 --> 45:26.014
I know he's sick, but still!

45:26.098 --> 45:29.143
Why did you discriminate Gang-tae
and prevent him from growing up properly?

45:31.854 --> 45:32.813
You're crazy.

45:36.984 --> 45:39.194
You just wait 60 years.

45:39.695 --> 45:42.489
Once I meet you up there, I'm going to--

45:42.573 --> 45:44.074
What are you going to do?

45:45.826 --> 45:46.660
My goodness.

45:47.995 --> 45:50.706
All mothers are sinners.

45:53.208 --> 45:56.545
But even so, cut your mother some slack.

45:59.548 --> 46:02.801
Do you think it was easy for a woman
to raise kids without a husband back then?

46:03.385 --> 46:04.428
My goodness.

46:05.721 --> 46:09.016
I only have a daughter,
but even I wanted to run away at times.

46:10.684 --> 46:13.770
But your mother
successfully raised two boys.

46:14.146 --> 46:16.440
On top of that, Sang-tae is one of a kind.

46:23.697 --> 46:27.159
You've been taking care of your brother,
so I'm sure you know

46:27.951 --> 46:30.287
how hard it must've been for her.

46:33.207 --> 46:36.335
Cheers to us. This is for you up there.

46:59.858 --> 47:02.402
My goodness, you're unbelievable.

47:02.945 --> 47:04.530
Do you feel better now?

47:06.782 --> 47:09.952
- Gang-tae came by and left just now.
- Why? Was he alone? What did he say?

47:12.329 --> 47:13.830
If you like him so much,

47:13.914 --> 47:17.251
why did you come home
on some other guy's back last night?

47:17.334 --> 47:20.087
Someone carried me home? Really?

47:21.755 --> 47:23.799
You know what? It's better not to know.

47:23.882 --> 47:26.260
Just don't bother remembering anything.
That'd be best.

47:34.893 --> 47:35.811
CEO LEE SANG-IN

47:35.936 --> 47:37.729
I'm the CEO of SangSangESang Publishers.

47:44.861 --> 47:46.947
- Mr. Lee.
- Yes?

47:47.447 --> 47:49.992
I want you to fix this!

47:56.498 --> 47:58.542
I must've lost my mind.

48:14.474 --> 48:16.393
Where are you? When are you coming?

48:16.560 --> 48:19.062
Hurry up and come home. I'm bored.

48:19.146 --> 48:21.023
Why are you ignoring me?
Are you kidding me?

48:23.483 --> 48:25.861
WATE.

48:28.155 --> 48:30.490
WIAT.

48:32.826 --> 48:36.204
WAIT.

49:12.783 --> 49:13.825
Why are you so late?

49:14.951 --> 49:17.371
- Why were you sleeping here?
- You told me to wait. Damn it.

49:19.915 --> 49:20.916
Did you drink?

49:22.376 --> 49:23.377
With whom?

49:24.127 --> 49:25.045
That two-faced bitch?

49:26.421 --> 49:27.673
No, not her.

49:28.256 --> 49:30.592
I drank with Jo Jae-su,
a chicken farm owner's son,

49:30.759 --> 49:32.928
and a live-in cook
who's over 60 years old.

49:34.096 --> 49:35.555
Did you meet people from online?

49:35.931 --> 49:36.973
"Meet people from online"?

49:39.393 --> 49:40.435
You're drunk.

49:42.479 --> 49:43.814
I was drunk,

49:44.314 --> 49:48.068
but the cab driver told me
he doesn't come here at night

49:48.527 --> 49:51.363
because this place is scary
and brings bad luck,

49:51.446 --> 49:53.115
and he told me to get out of the cab.

49:53.699 --> 49:56.827
So I walked all the way here,
and I'm almost sober now.

50:01.373 --> 50:02.499
Then let's drink some more.

50:02.582 --> 50:05.127
No, forget it. This is
just the right amount of tipsiness.

50:06.253 --> 50:07.462
I want to drink.

50:08.380 --> 50:09.297
No, you can't.

50:10.132 --> 50:11.633
You never do things in moderation.

50:12.759 --> 50:15.595
If both of us end up getting drunk,

50:18.390 --> 50:19.266
it'll be bad.

50:20.642 --> 50:21.476
Why?

50:22.102 --> 50:23.603
Are you scared I might come onto you?

50:25.689 --> 50:27.983
- Stop acting up.
- Did you just hit me?

50:28.859 --> 50:30.068
You hurt me with a knife.

50:33.572 --> 50:35.198
You have good comebacks when you're drunk.

50:42.956 --> 50:44.833
I want to pull out your safety pin.

50:46.793 --> 50:47.711
Close your eyes.

50:49.004 --> 50:49.963
Why?

50:50.547 --> 50:51.465
Just close your eyes.

50:52.799 --> 50:54.342
You're so cliché.

51:04.352 --> 51:05.520
Here. Open your eyes.

51:09.149 --> 51:10.942
What is this piece of crap?

51:11.151 --> 51:12.319
A nightmare catcher.

51:15.530 --> 51:18.074
If you sleep with this in your hand,

51:18.992 --> 51:21.703
it collects your nightmares in its basket

51:22.120 --> 51:23.455
and eats it up overnight.

51:25.791 --> 51:27.417
Then you'll be able to sleep comfortably.

51:29.628 --> 51:30.879
How childish.

51:32.130 --> 51:33.632
I brought it from home today.

51:34.925 --> 51:37.844
- It used to be my brother's.
- What? It's used?

51:39.095 --> 51:41.389
I made it myself.

51:46.228 --> 51:47.938
If it's handmade, I guess it's worth it.

51:49.231 --> 51:51.316
This guy's name is Mang-tae.

51:54.027 --> 51:57.239
Don't tell me you named it Mang-tae
because you're Gang-tae,

51:57.614 --> 51:59.157
and your brother is Sang-tae.

52:03.328 --> 52:04.162
The three of us

52:05.455 --> 52:06.540
are brothers.

52:09.167 --> 52:10.585
Unbelievable.

52:13.964 --> 52:15.090
To be honest,

52:17.050 --> 52:19.928
my brother also has nightmares
just like you.

52:23.056 --> 52:24.516
He's been having nightmares

52:26.268 --> 52:27.477
ever since our mom passed away.

52:36.736 --> 52:38.280
My brother felt tormented,

52:40.156 --> 52:42.200
but there was nothing I could do.

52:46.329 --> 52:47.372
All I could do

52:48.540 --> 52:50.417
was make him this silly doll.

52:55.547 --> 52:58.341
Well, it's kind of cute
now that I take a close look at it.

53:01.094 --> 53:03.597
- Do you want it?
- Yes, I want it.

53:05.599 --> 53:06.683
Okay.

53:07.893 --> 53:08.935
Good night.

53:25.577 --> 53:26.453
Mang-tae.

53:45.096 --> 53:46.306
Sang-tae.

53:47.057 --> 53:48.099
Are you sleeping?

53:50.310 --> 53:51.269
Are you really sleeping?

53:56.107 --> 53:58.985
Gosh, you reek of alcohol.
I'm... I'm so upset.

53:59.069 --> 54:02.072
My gosh, you... You stink.
You reek of alcohol.

54:04.741 --> 54:08.161
Sang-tae, let's have jjamppong someday

54:08.703 --> 54:10.497
at that place we used to go with Mom.

54:10.580 --> 54:13.249
- It's at the entrance of the market.
- Yes.

54:15.251 --> 54:18.505
You used to love the jjamppong there.

54:18.588 --> 54:22.592
No, you... You were the one who loved it.

54:24.970 --> 54:26.680
No, you always--

54:26.763 --> 54:29.891
"It has chili pepper and mussels inside.
The broth tastes amazing.

54:29.975 --> 54:31.977
I want to have it every day, Mom."
You told her that.

54:32.060 --> 54:35.313
That's why she bought us that jjamppong

54:35.814 --> 54:37.399
every time the market opened.

54:37.983 --> 54:40.610
"It's spicy but tasty."

54:41.194 --> 54:43.989
Sang-tae, jjamppong is spicy but tasty.

54:44.614 --> 54:45.991
It makes me want to eat it again.

54:46.074 --> 54:47.158
HARIMGAK

54:48.743 --> 54:49.619
The jjamppong is here.

54:51.287 --> 54:52.330
- Thank you.
- Sure.

54:52.414 --> 54:54.332
Here. Eat up.

54:55.625 --> 54:57.252
What about you, Mom?

54:57.335 --> 54:58.586
I'm not hungry.

55:00.046 --> 55:00.880
Eat up.

55:02.382 --> 55:03.258
It's... It's spicy.

55:03.341 --> 55:06.011
- Is it spicy? Drink some water.
- It's spicy.

55:09.180 --> 55:10.056
It's spicy.

55:10.473 --> 55:12.851
My gosh, it's pouring.

55:16.855 --> 55:18.857
You'll catch a cold. Are you okay?

55:31.578 --> 55:32.829
Gang-tae, what are you doing?

55:34.748 --> 55:37.917
- Gang-tae, get over here. It's raining.
- Gang-tae, get over here.

55:38.001 --> 55:38.835
Come on.

55:46.760 --> 55:48.636
Look at you. You're all wet.

55:48.928 --> 55:51.347
Let's go home and get you changed.

55:52.348 --> 55:53.433
Be careful.

55:54.726 --> 55:57.145
Gang-tae, should we
eat jjamppong again tomorrow?

55:57.395 --> 55:58.229
"Jjamppong"?

56:01.149 --> 56:03.485
It's hard to lose five kilograms.
But I tried so hard.

56:03.610 --> 56:06.112
I didn't drink Coke or eat rice,
and I lost five kilograms.

56:06.196 --> 56:08.364
I lost five kilograms. It was amazing.

56:15.497 --> 56:18.666
We... We need to listen to our mom.

56:18.750 --> 56:20.752
We need to listen to our mom.

56:20.835 --> 56:23.630
We need to listen to our mom
in order to be a good person.

56:24.255 --> 56:27.133
Our mom knows everything.

56:27.884 --> 56:30.845
Our mom knows... She knows everything.

56:31.346 --> 56:33.765
Don't catch a cold. Don't drink Coke.

57:03.586 --> 57:05.046
My adorable son.

57:08.258 --> 57:09.759
I'm so sorry for everything.

57:23.273 --> 57:24.274
Sang-tae.

57:25.525 --> 57:26.484
Yes?

57:34.617 --> 57:35.994
I miss Mom.

57:37.829 --> 57:38.746
Yes.

57:40.915 --> 57:43.460
I want jjamppong, too.

57:46.171 --> 57:49.299
I want jjamppong every single day.

58:25.251 --> 58:27.045
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

58:27.295 --> 58:28.546
Everyone badmouths you

58:28.630 --> 58:31.341
saying you made Ms. Kang Eun-ja collapse.

58:31.424 --> 58:32.884
But I never badmouthed you.

58:33.468 --> 58:35.929
To be honest, that woman isn't sane.

58:36.012 --> 58:38.223
She always wears the shawl she got
from her late daughter

58:38.306 --> 58:39.974
and pretends like she's rich.

58:40.058 --> 58:42.477
- That darn geezer. Move.
- I really don't think--

58:43.770 --> 58:44.604
Ms. Ko.

58:46.105 --> 58:47.982
- She hit me again.
- Darn it.

58:51.444 --> 58:52.320
Oh, gosh.

58:53.279 --> 58:54.906
Emergency.

58:55.865 --> 58:58.368
We have a situation. What should we do?

58:58.451 --> 58:59.869
- What is it?
- What's wrong?

59:00.954 --> 59:03.081
Will you please be quiet?

59:03.665 --> 59:04.499
Be silent.

59:05.625 --> 59:07.418
Are you trying to agitate the patients?

59:08.044 --> 59:09.796
Be careful when you use
the word "emergency."

59:10.088 --> 59:13.132
Ms. Ko is here. I think she came
not knowing her class got canceled.

59:13.716 --> 59:17.178
She had this look on her face
and went to find the director.

59:17.762 --> 59:19.847
- Didn't you call her?
- Didn't you?

59:20.181 --> 59:21.724
Why didn't you?

59:23.017 --> 59:24.310
- What?
- You guys are close.

59:24.394 --> 59:25.228
No, they're not!

59:25.812 --> 59:28.606
Wait. Wait a minute.

59:28.690 --> 59:33.069
Does that mean
no one called and told Ms. Ko

59:33.152 --> 59:35.196
that her fairy tale class got canceled?

59:35.780 --> 59:36.948
What's wrong with you?

59:37.031 --> 59:39.867
She found out through the notice board.
She must be furious right now.

59:39.951 --> 59:41.119
I'll go find her.

59:42.620 --> 59:45.415
I used to run marathons when I was young.

59:45.957 --> 59:47.792
But one day, my knees got infected.

59:48.501 --> 59:52.463
I should've gotten some rest,
but I just ran a marathon again.

59:54.841 --> 59:57.760
In the end, my cartilage got ruined,
and I ended up with metal pins.

59:57.844 --> 59:59.804
Now, it's hard for me
to even walk properly.

01:00:02.015 --> 01:00:05.727
Don't make the same mistake I did
and try to run when you can't even walk.

01:00:11.858 --> 01:00:14.569
When you're tired, get some rest.
When you're sad, go ahead and cry.

01:00:16.696 --> 01:00:18.656
It's okay to take a break.

01:00:19.240 --> 01:00:20.325
Then one day,

01:00:21.701 --> 01:00:24.621
there will surely come a day
when you'll be able to run again.

01:00:25.872 --> 01:00:28.291
I bet your daughter is cheering you on.

01:00:31.085 --> 01:00:34.213
That darn geezer. How dare he cancel
my class without telling me?

01:00:35.590 --> 01:00:36.674
There he is.

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:40.637
Darn, did he take drugs or something?
Why is he so fast?

01:00:47.560 --> 01:00:48.394
Ms. Ko!

01:00:55.777 --> 01:00:57.028
Wait here for a second.

01:00:59.113 --> 01:01:00.448
Let me take you back to your room.

01:01:03.868 --> 01:01:04.702
I'm sorry.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:09.624
I'm guessing I put you
in a difficult position.

01:01:10.708 --> 01:01:12.502
You didn't just put me
in a difficult position.

01:01:12.919 --> 01:01:14.045
I got fired.

01:01:14.837 --> 01:01:15.838
Hey.

01:01:16.422 --> 01:01:17.715
How will you compensate for this?

01:01:28.810 --> 01:01:29.644
This is expensive.

01:01:31.562 --> 01:01:34.315
- I want it.
- But that's...

01:01:34.399 --> 01:01:35.483
Let me have this.

01:01:38.111 --> 01:01:41.406
You told me you're sorry.
Then you should compensate for the damage.

01:01:41.948 --> 01:01:43.449
That's what you call a sincere apology.

01:01:53.668 --> 01:01:54.502
Give it back.

01:01:58.297 --> 01:01:59.590
Take it.

01:02:03.261 --> 01:02:05.263
I've had it for more than enough.

01:02:17.400 --> 01:02:18.484
Mr. Moon.

01:02:19.819 --> 01:02:20.737
Yes?

01:02:21.779 --> 01:02:23.573
The burden is finally gone.

01:02:38.171 --> 01:02:39.338
Isn't it hot?

01:02:39.964 --> 01:02:41.466
I bet your neck is sweating.

01:02:42.133 --> 01:02:45.511
If you want to be fashionable,
you must be uncomfortable and stubborn.

01:02:48.848 --> 01:02:50.933
My brother is immersed
in one of your books these days.

01:02:51.893 --> 01:02:52.935
I know.

01:02:53.478 --> 01:02:54.645
The Cheerful Dog.

01:03:01.694 --> 01:03:03.112
"Once upon a time,

01:03:03.196 --> 01:03:08.201
there lived a dog that was
very good at hiding his emotions.

01:03:09.410 --> 01:03:11.871
The dog was tied beneath a shade tree.

01:03:11.954 --> 01:03:14.373
He always wagged his tail and acted cute.

01:03:14.457 --> 01:03:17.835
So he got the name, "The Cheerful Dog,"
because he was as cheerful as springtime.

01:03:18.127 --> 01:03:22.381
The dog always had lots of fun
with the village kids during the day.

01:03:22.632 --> 01:03:23.758
But every night,

01:03:23.841 --> 01:03:28.971
he'd moan and whine
when no one was around.

01:03:29.680 --> 01:03:34.143
That's because
he wanted to cut off the leash

01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:38.523
and freely run around
out in the spring field.

01:03:39.023 --> 01:03:41.359
However, he couldn't.

01:03:41.442 --> 01:03:44.237
And that's why he cried every night.

01:03:44.695 --> 01:03:47.490
Every single night.

01:03:48.324 --> 01:03:49.242
One day,

01:03:49.325 --> 01:03:53.788
a voice inside him asked the Cheerful Dog.

01:03:54.580 --> 01:03:59.544
'Hey, why don't you just cut off the leash
and run away?'

01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:02.255
And this is what the Cheerful Dog said..."

01:04:03.464 --> 01:04:07.176
"I've been tied up for way too long.

01:04:08.719 --> 01:04:10.972
So I forgot how to cut myself free."

01:04:24.360 --> 01:04:25.653
You did great, Mun-yeong.

01:04:27.738 --> 01:04:28.823
What did I do?

01:04:30.074 --> 01:04:31.868
You helped her cut herself free.

01:05:02.106 --> 01:05:03.149
You will

01:05:06.777 --> 01:05:09.405
end up like your mother.

01:05:10.781 --> 01:05:14.660
You won't be able to escape.

01:05:17.371 --> 01:05:18.205
No.

01:05:20.041 --> 01:05:21.083
I'm different.

01:06:35.449 --> 01:06:36.534
Your...

01:06:38.577 --> 01:06:40.162
- Your hair--
- I...

01:06:40.997 --> 01:06:42.456
cut off my leash.

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:01.517
PATIENT ROOM 201-208

01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:15.174
It's all done.

01:09:22.616 --> 01:09:23.576
How do I look?

01:09:27.121 --> 01:09:28.080
You look pretty.

01:09:59.069 --> 01:10:01.947
SPECIAL THANKS TO BAE HAE-SUN
FOR MAKING A GUEST APPEARANCE

01:10:39.526 --> 01:10:40.444
I'm very pretty.

01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:42.905
I'm just like your brother.

01:10:42.988 --> 01:10:44.782
Longer hair suits you better.

01:10:44.865 --> 01:10:46.951
Why did she cut it? Why?

01:10:47.034 --> 01:10:48.118
Chew on this.

01:10:48.702 --> 01:10:50.454
Why do you think she lied?

01:10:50.537 --> 01:10:53.165
It seems like something strange
is happening at our hospital.

01:10:54.041 --> 01:10:55.251
That woman

01:10:56.293 --> 01:10:57.294
is dead.

01:10:58.045 --> 01:10:59.880
But she's here.

01:11:01.131 --> 01:11:02.716
Safety pin and bomb.

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:06.220
You're patient, and I'm volatile.

01:11:06.303 --> 01:11:08.055
Could you take a photo of us?

01:11:08.264 --> 01:11:11.642
According to Mr. Lee, I sell one more book
every time I smile at a fan.

01:11:11.725 --> 01:11:13.352
An author only needs to write well.

01:11:13.435 --> 01:11:15.062
She's not a celebrity.

01:11:15.145 --> 01:11:17.147
- Are you jealous?
- Jealous, my ass.

01:11:20.317 --> 01:11:21.277
"Offer"?

01:11:21.944 --> 01:11:24.405
But if I give all my stuff to people
who need them,

01:11:26.240 --> 01:11:28.033
what will I have left?

01:11:31.328 --> 01:11:33.956
Subtitle translation by Ja-won Lee
